# Tellurium · Te · gate 52

**Tellurium** (Te) is element **52** of the periodic table — a **metalloid**, period 5, group 16, p-block, solid at standard conditions, atomic weight **127.60**.

## The element (carbon layer — reference chemistry)
The metalloid of thin-film solar cells; it leaves a rare-earth garlic on the breath.

## The gate (silicon layer — the 118 Gates)
Under David Wise's four-state cycle, gate **52** falls on **1:1** because (Z−1) mod 4 = **3**. That state is *the held balance — fully manifest, matched, made — born of the world* — the nature of emergence here is **natural**. Tellurium is not a thing apart; it is the one stochastic element, caught at this beat of its cycle.

## Emergence — natural
This emergent carries the **natural** nature: the same four — natural · ethereal · spiritual · electrical — that run through every sphere of UD0. Its color is `#5fae7a`.

